 "pdf": "ads8555.pdf",
 "pages": "p.3 (pin configuration), p.4-6 (pin functions), p.10 (BVDD 2.7-5.5 V), p.11 (serial timing: tCONV 1.26 us max, tD2 FS low to SDO active 12 ns, tD3 SCLK rising to new data 15 ns, tD4 FS high to 3-state 10 ns, SDI latched on SCLK falling), p.12 (Figure 1), p.24 (Table 2, serial interface: data change on SCLK rising, read on falling, SDO_A order A0 A1 B0 B1 C0 C1), p.25 (Table 3 twos complement), p.26 (serial: control register contents required with each read access, C16 = 1 for a full update), p.29-30 (control register map, default 0x000003FF)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog side: +/-4 VREF / +/-2 VREF bipolar inputs (RANGE pin or RANGE_x bits), HVDD/HVSS, internal reference, REFDAC (C[9:0]), reference buffers and decoupling pins; every channel gives the 0 V code (twos, 0000h)",
  "only the serial interface (PAR/SER high) is modeled, with all six results on SDO_A (SEL_A = 1, SEL_B = SEL_C = 0: 96 SCLKs). SDO_B/SDO_C splits, daisy-chain inputs (DCEN/DCIN_x) are not modeled; DB9/DB10 are never driven. The parallel interface (word or byte mode with HBEN, CR written by two 16-bit or four 8-bit WR accesses) is not modeled",
  "each frame restarts the output at CH_A0; reading the results over several shorter frames is not modeled (all results are 0 anyway)",
  "CR read-out: READ_EN is not stored (reads back 0) and C16 (C23:0_EN) is not stored; with READ_EN the next frame outputs the 32-bit CR instead of the results",
  "software mode: CH_A/CH_B/CH_C (C31-C29, default 0) enable channel pairs for the next conversion and SEQ (C23) selects sequential starts with CONVST_B/C; not modeled - CONVST_A converts all six channels in both modes",
  "hardware mode: CONVST_B / CONVST_C start their channel pairs separately; only CONVST_A is read (tie them together)",
  "conversion clock: internal clock tCONV max used; external XCLK (CLKSEL), CLKOUT_EN, auto-NAP (A_NAP, wake-up time), per-pair power-down PD_x are not modeled",
  "STBY powers the device down (modeled as powerdown); RESET resets CR (modeled); BUSY/INT polarity and INT mode from CR C21/C20 (INT clears at the first read access, modeled as FS falling)"
 ],
